Here, $A=\left\{x: x^{2}-x+2\gt 0\right\}=R\left(\begin{array}{l}
\because x^{2}-x+2=x^{2}-x+\frac{1}{4}+\frac{7}{4} \\
=\left(x-\frac{1}{2}\right)^{2}+\frac{7}{4} \geq \frac{7}{4}
\end{array}\right)$
and $B=\left\{x: x^{2}-4 x+3 \leq 0\right\}=\{x:(x-1)(x-3) \leq 0)=[1,3]$
Hence, $A \cap B=R \cap[1,3]=[1,3]$

Since, $n(A \cap B)=99n((A \times B) \cap(B \times A))$
\begin{aligned}
&=n((A \cap B) \times(B \cap A)) \\
&=n(A \cap B) \cdot n(B \cap A) \\
&=n(A \cap B) \cdot n(A \cap B)=99 \cdot 99=(99)^{2}
\end{aligned}

